/*
Chef has forgotten his ice cream cone in the sun, and it is melting.

Currently, there is XX grams of ice cream in his cone, and every minute that the cone is left out, YY grams of ice cream melt and are lost.

If Chef comes back after NN minutes, how much ice cream is still left for him?
Input Format

    The first line of input will contain a single integer TT, denoting the number of test cases.
    The first and only line of each test case contains 33 integers - XX, YY and NN.

Output Format

For each test case, output on a new line the amount of ice cream left after NN minutes.
Constraints

    1≤T≤1001≤T≤100
    1≤X,Y,N≤1001≤X,Y,N≤100

Sample 1:
Input
Output

3
5 1 2
5 1 7
50 5 9

3
0
5

Explanation:

Test Case 1 : Chef comes back after 22 minutes, and in that time 22 grams of ice cream have melted, leaving him 33 grams.

Test Case 2 : The ice cream completely melts in 55 minutes, and thus is gone by the time Chef returns.

*/
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int main() {
	// your code goes here
	int t;
	cin>>t;
	
	while(t--) {
	    int x,y,n;
	    cin>>x>>y>>n;
	    
	    int k = x - y*n;
	    
	    if(k>0) {
	        cout<<k<<endl;
	    }
	    else{
	        cout<<0<<endl;
	    }
	}

}
